jobs.description:
In line with our expectations, we expect our team members to be passionate about their work, to act with honesty and integrity, and to have a healthy dose of enthusiasm. The desired skills for the Quality Control Employee are also:
*  At least MBO level of working and thinking;
* 2-3 years work experience as a Quality Control Employee in a food company;
* Flexibility: working in four overlapping shifts, with Saturdays occasionally forming part of the working week;
* Fluency in spoken and written English; Dutch is an advantage;
* Knowledge of HACCP and GFSI;
* Strong communication skills, persuasive and decisive;
* Works accurately and is proactive;
* You are proficient in Excel and Word.

The New Plant - At The New Plant we produce Beyond Meats plant-based protein products for customers in Europe, the middle East and parts of Africa. Beyond Meat has been partnering with McDonalds sinds 2021 and supplies the vegetarian patty for the McPlant. Within your team, you will be working alongside three Quality Control Employee, a Quality Control Supervisor and a Quality Control Manager, and you will collaborate with two Quality Assurance Assistants.

Can your colleagues in production count on spotless and hygienic workspaces? Do you enjoy staying active on the job? Then you can quickly start working as a cleaner or industrial cleaner at Luiten! Your full-time workday starts around 9:00 or 10:00 AM. You’ll change into your work attire, grab your cleaning materials and equipment, and begin moving between the various production areas with your high-pressure cleaner.
Not only will you thoroughly clean the production spaces, but you’ll also ensure that the machines used to process and package meat—and all related materials—are meticulously cleaned. You take care of your own work, following HACCP and hygiene regulations carefully. In addition to cleaning, you make sure that every area is safe to enter and ready for use.
No need for an activity tracker here, as you’ll definitely get plenty of daily movement in this role! Together with your friendly, multicultural team, you’ll ensure production can start on time and in a clean environment.

- You are available full-time from Monday till Friday;
- Overtime doesn’t wear you out—instead, it makes your wallet fuller;
- You speak Dutch or English, essential for safety on the work floor;
- Some experience with cleaning and/or sanitation is a plus.

Are you experienced in a warehouse and ready to take the next step into a leadership role? Or do you already have some experience in supervising colleagues and want to further develop yourself as a team leader? Then this is your opportunity! Within a fast-growing and international logistics environment, you will have the opportunity to further develop your leadership skills and  take on more responsibility step by step.

As a (junior) Warehouse Team Leader, you will work alongside an experienced team and supervise a group of 10 to 12 employees. You will be visibly present on the work floor, supporting the daily coordination of operations. You work closely with the Supervisor and be given the space to grow in your role.

Your responsibilities include:

- Supporting the supervision and guidance of warehouse employees;
- Working on the floor to ensure smooth daily operations;
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and discussing them with your manager;
- Contributing to the improvement of work processes;
- Monitoring basic safety and quality regulations;
- Working with simple reports and developing basic Excel skills.

We are primarily looking for someone with the right motivation and ambition to grow into a leadership role within logistics. In addition, you have:

- Experience in a warehouse or logistics environment;
- Interest in supervising or guiding colleagues;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Basic knowledge of Excel or willingness to learn;
- A proactive and eager-to-learn attitude;
- Availability to work full-time in a two-shift system.

Have you not yet held a full team leader position, but do you have ambition and some initial experience in leading others? We strongly encourage you to apply.

Work in a international production team and help make high-quality products. You'll operate machines, check quality, and keep everything running smoothly. As a Production Employee, your tasks are broad and varied. While some tasks are repetitive, employees rotate weekly between different workstations and responsibilities. This ensures that you remain widely deployable, engaged, and continuously developing new skills.

What you'll do:

- Operating and monitoring production machines;
- Performing quality checks and completing required documentation;
- Counting, stamping, and registering production time;
- Preparing finished products and orders for shipping;
- Keeping your workspace clean, organized, and safe;
- Reporting deviations, malfunctions, or quality issues to your team leader.

You will work in three shifts:

- 06:00 – 14:00
- 14:00 – 22:00
- 22:00 – 06:00

- Good knowledge of the English language;
- Ability to work accurately and precisely – this is the most important requirement;
- Basic computer skills (data entry, forms, registrations);
- A focused mindset with the ability to work quickly and efficiently;
- Flexibility and willingness to learn and rotate between workstations;
- Availability and motivation to work in a 3- as well as a 2-shift system;
